messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFor each integer $n$, let $f(n)$ be the sum of the elements of the $n$th row (i.e. the row with $n+1$ elements) of Pascal's triangle minus the sum of all the elements from previous rows. For example, \\[f(2) = \\underbrace{(1 + 2 + 1)}_{\\text{2nd row}} - \\underbrace{(1 + 1 + 1)}_{\\text{0th and 1st rows}} = 1. \\]What is the minimum value of $f(n)$ for $n \\ge 2015$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"6fb9acf211b83aba186662be6b542d8b698c0f8c19f8b5488310a01442a3e9b4"},"seconds":7.622418642044067,"seed":156702995724720249,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( f(n) \\) for \\( n \\ge 2015 \\), we first need to understand the properties of Pascal's triangle and the sum of its elements.\n\nThe sum of the elements in the \\( n \\)th row of Pascal's triangle (where the top row is the 0th row) is \\( 2^n \\). This is a well-known property of Pascal's triangle.\n\nGiven the definition of \\( f(n) \\), we can write:\n\\[ f(n) = \\text{sum of the elements in the } n\\text{th row} - \\text{sum of the elements in all previous rows} \\]\n\\[ f(n) = 2^n - \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} 2^k \\]\n\nThe sum of the first \\( n \\) powers of 2 is:\n\\[ \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} 2^k = 2^n - 1 \\]\n\nThus, we can substitute this into the expression for \\( f(n) \\):\n\\[ f(n) = 2^n - (2^n - 1) = 1 \\]\n\nThis result is independent of \\( n \\), meaning \\( f(n) = 1 \\) for all \\( n \\ge 0 \\).\n\nTherefore, for \\( n \\ge 2015 \\), the minimum value of \\( f(n) \\) is:\n\\[ \\boxed{1} \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"counting_and_probability:226"}
